2224 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Flame arrestors are safety\055critical devices used in industrial pipelines to prevent flame propagation\056 Evaluating their performance requires comparing pressure drop data across product configurations\054 test conditions\054 and computational fluid dynamics \050CFD\051 simulations\054 which is a process that was previously fragmented across disconnected spreadsheets with no standardized schema or validation\056\nArrestorIQ is a cross\055platform desktop and mobile application built for Emerson that unifies arrestor product data management under a single validated platform\056 The application ingests and validates test\054 CFD\054 and bill\055of\055materials data via the Emerson Data Interchange \050EDI\051 standard\054 implemented as a purpose\055built Haxe\055compiled parsing engine that runs natively in both JavaScript and Python\056 Engineers can import new data through a drag\055and\055drop interface\054 browse a catalog of product configurations\054 compare regression models across multiple products\054 and inspect the full hierarchical BOM tree with deeplinks into Emerson\047s IAS system\056 A fully automated CI\057CD pipeline integrated with Emerson\047s Azure DevOps infrastructure triggers verified releases from git tags\054 making the tool self\055sustaining post\055handoff\056)
     /K [ 16 ]
     /P 2225 0 R
     /Pg 2192 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

